  "acceptance": [
    "all auth mail is durably queued before request success and never synchronously delivered by the Web runtime",
    "auth mail uses a dedicated auth.mail_outbox and cannot be claimed by the generic Kafka outbox worker",
    "recipient, subject, body and bearer tokens are AES-256-GCM encrypted at rest under a dedicated server-side key",
    "pc_auth_mail_runtime is a distinct NOINHERIT NOSUPERUSER NOBYPASSRLS PostgreSQL login with no role memberships and no INSERT/DELETE authority",
    "mail worker is a separate non-public runtime process on the existing REG.RU host and can scale through SKIP LOCKED leases",
    "only the mail worker receives REG.RU SMTP credentials; API receives only the outbox encryption key; Web receives neither",
    "SMTP authority is fixed to mail.hosting.reg.ru:465 with certificate verification and TLS 1.2 or newer",
    "SMTP credentials and mail outbox/database keys are stored only under the REG.RU server-side root secret authority and never in GitHub Secrets",
    "retries use bounded exponential backoff, deterministic Message-ID, expiry and terminal dead-letter state",
    "production release fails closed if required auth-mail secret authorities, worker readiness or database principal boundary are absent",
    "SPF, DKIM and DMARC are required production evidence before auth-mail architecture is declared complete",
